    - Choose 1-3 feature pairs; for each pair, pick a random row or column through the body and a random direction
    - For each pair, add both the tab and its complementary notch on opposite edges of that row/column (this is the output state)
    - Derive the input by undoing the transformation -- remove every output-side complementary feature (delete each added tab, restore each carved notch)
